// Browser sync bridges a compromised personal profile into a corporate session by running personal and corporate
// browser profiles side-by-side on the same managed endpoint. Native EDR telemetry cannot see which account is
// signed into a given Chrome/Edge profile, so this uses the observable host artifact: multiple distinct
// --profile-directory values launched on the same device in a short window, a precondition for cross-profile
// sync of saved sessions/credentials described in the attack chain.
// Tightened: fixed a broken final projection (it was re-deriving a bucket from now() instead of
// referencing the actual grouped bucket), and raised the profile-diversity bar from >1 to >=3.
// A single extra profile alongside "Default" is normal, common work/personal separation on one
// machine; requiring at least three distinct profiles active in the same hour is a materially
// less common pattern and a better proxy for the multi-identity juggling this opportunity targets.
DeviceProcessEvents
| where FileName in~ ("chrome.exe", "msedge.exe")
| where ProcessCommandLine has "profile-directory"
| extend ProfileDir = extract(@'profile-directory="?([^"\s]+)', 1, ProcessCommandLine)
| where isnotempty(ProfileDir)
| summarize ProfileDirs = make_set(ProfileDir, 10), Launches = count() by DeviceId, TimeBucket = bin(Timestamp, 1h)
| where array_length(ProfileDirs) >= 3
| project TimeBucket, DeviceId, ProfileDirs, Launches
| sort by TimeBucket desc